{
  "slug": "rationalise-conjugate-am",
  "title": "Two terms below: multiply by the conjugate",
  "level": "AM",
  "topic": "Surds",
  "minutes": 2,
  "kind": "clip",
  "theme": "chalk",
  "question": "Rationalize the denominator of $\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}$.",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "equation-steps",
      "heading": "Multiply by the conjugate",
      "scroll": true,
      "steps": [
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "id": "q1", "tex": "\\dfrac{2}{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-d}{\\sqrt{5}\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-s}{+}\\sqrt{3}}}" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "id": "p1", "tex": "\\text{Plan: }\\dfrac{\\cdots}{\\text{no surd}}", "hl": "sky" }
          ],
          "corner": true
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "id": "m1", "tex": "=\\dfrac{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-t}{2}}{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-d}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}}" },
            {
              "id": "m2",
              "tex": "\\times\\dfrac{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-t}{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}}{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-d}{\\sqrt{5}\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-s}{-}\\sqrt{3}}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            {
              "id": "k1",
              "tex": "=\\dfrac{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-t}{2(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3})}}{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-d}{(\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-a}{\\sqrt{5}}+\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-b}{\\sqrt{3}})(\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-a}{\\sqrt{5}}-\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-b}{\\sqrt{3}})}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            {
              "id": "e1",
              "tex": "=\\dfrac{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-t}{2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{3}}}{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-d}{(\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-a}{\\sqrt{5}})^2-(\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-b}{\\sqrt{3}})^2}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "id": "f1", "tex": "=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{3}}{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-d}{5-3}}" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "id": "h1", "tex": "=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{3}}{\\htmlClass{lsn-pc-d}{2}}" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "id": "g1", "tex": "=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}-\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{3}}{2}" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tokens": [
            { "id": "ans", "tex": "=\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}", "hl": "emerald" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Rationalize the denominator of two over root five plus root three.",
          "asks": ["What is the denominator?", "What does rationalize mean?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 0 }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Rationalizing means removing the surd from the bottom of the fraction. Here the bottom has two terms.",
          "asks": ["Why remove the surd from the bottom?", "Which part is the bottom?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "q1", "inside": "d", "tone": "orange", "on": "from the bottom" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "So the plan: the same value, written with no surd in the bottom.",
          "asks": ["Does the value change?", "Why keep the same value?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "step": 1, "on": "the same value" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "With two terms below, multiplying by root five alone still leaves a surd below.",
          "asks": ["Why not multiply by root five?", "Why not root three?"],
          "aside": {
            "text": "Why not times root five?",
            "slug": "surds-why-conjugate",
            "read": [
              "Try $\\times\\dfrac{\\sqrt5}{\\sqrt5}$: the bottom becomes $(\\sqrt5+\\sqrt3)\\sqrt5 = 5+\\sqrt{15}$.",
              "A surd is still there: $\\sqrt{15}$.",
              "Try the bottom itself: $(\\sqrt5+\\sqrt3)^2 = 8+2\\sqrt{15}$. Still a surd.",
              "Only $(\\sqrt5+\\sqrt3)(\\sqrt5-\\sqrt3)$ loses every surd.",
              "Its two middle terms, $-\\sqrt{15}$ and $+\\sqrt{15}$, cancel.",
              "**Two terms below: multiply by the conjugate.**"
            ]
          },
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "q1", "inside": "d", "tone": "orange" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "We multiply by the conjugate: the same pair, with only the middle sign flipped.",
          "asks": ["What is a conjugate?", "Which sign is the middle sign?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "note", "text": "Conjugate: change only the middle sign", "near": "q1", "on": "the same pair" },
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "q1", "inside": "s", "tone": "orange", "on": "the middle sign" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Why the conjugate: a pair times its conjugate gives two squares, and squaring a surd clears the root.",
          "asks": ["Why does the conjugate clear the surd?", "Why not square the bottom?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "q1", "inside": "d", "tone": "sky" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Write the fraction again, then times root five minus root three, over root five minus root three.",
          "asks": ["Why write the fraction again?", "Why put the conjugate on the top too?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "token": "m1" },
            { "do": "write", "token": "m2", "on": "then times root" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Plus becomes minus, and only the middle sign changes. Root five stays root five.",
          "asks": ["Do I change both signs?", "Why does root five stay?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "m2", "inside": "s", "tone": "orange" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "We multiply the top and the bottom by the same thing, so the value does not change.",
          "asks": ["Why does the value stay the same?", "Can I multiply only the bottom?"],
          "aside": {
            "text": "Why does the value stay the same?",
            "slug": "surds-times-one",
            "read": [
              "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt5-\\sqrt3}{\\sqrt5-\\sqrt3}$ has the same top and bottom.",
              "So it equals $1$.",
              "Multiplying by $1$ changes nothing.",
              "Multiplying only the bottom would change the value.",
              "**Top and bottom, always both.**"
            ]
          },
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "m2", "tone": "sky" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Multiply the top with the top: two times root five minus root three.",
          "asks": ["Why is there a bracket?", "Do I expand it now?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "m1", "inside": "t", "tone": "orange" },
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "m2", "inside": "t", "tone": "orange", "on": "with the top" },
            { "do": "write", "token": "k1", "on": "two times root" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "And the bottom with the bottom: root five plus root three, times root five minus root three.",
          "asks": ["Why keep the two brackets?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "m1", "inside": "d", "tone": "sky" },
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "m2", "inside": "d", "tone": "sky", "on": "with the bottom" },
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "k1", "inside": "d", "tone": "sky", "on": "root five plus" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "The bottom is A plus B, times A minus B. That always equals A squared minus B squared.",
          "asks": ["Where does this rule come from?", "What are A and B here?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "k1", "inside": "d", "tone": "sky" },
            { "do": "note", "text": "(a + b)(a − b) = a² − b²", "near": "k1", "on": "That always equals" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Here A is root five, and B is root three.",
          "asks": ["Which one is A?", "Does the order matter?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "k1", "inside": "a", "tone": "orange" },
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "k1", "inside": "b", "tone": "sky", "on": "B is root" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Expand the top: two root five minus two root three. The bottom: root five squared, minus root three squared.",
          "asks": ["How do I expand the top?", "Where did the middle terms go?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "token": "e1" },
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "e1", "inside": "a", "tone": "orange", "on": "The bottom: root" },
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "e1", "inside": "b", "tone": "sky", "on": "minus root three" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "A surd times itself is the number inside. So root five squared is five, and root three squared is three.",
          "asks": ["Why is root five squared five?", "Is root two squared four?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "e1", "inside": "d", "tone": "sky" },
            { "do": "write", "token": "f1", "on": "So root five" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Five minus three is two. The bottom is now a number with no surd.",
          "asks": ["Is two still a surd?", "Why is this the plan?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "highlight", "token": "f1", "inside": "d", "tone": "orange" },
            { "do": "write", "token": "h1", "on": "is two" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Split the fraction: each term over two.",
          "asks": ["Why split the fraction?", "Can I leave it as one fraction?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "token": "g1" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide each term by two: two root five over two is root five. So the answer is root five minus root three.",
          "asks": ["Is there still a surd in the bottom?", "Can I check with a calculator?"],
          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "token": "ans", "on": "So the answer" },
            { "do": "mark", "kind": "box", "token": "ans", "on": "root five minus" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
